Only in the reverse direction (that is, savefiles from the patch won't
work properly in unpatched versions, in this respect only). You'd just
need to add 'HLifesaved &= ~FROMOUTSIDE;' to the lifesaving routine to
make it one-time (and make the appropriate changes to the property's
shotrcuts in youprop.h).

(If you ever added any _permanent_ sources of intrinsic lifesaving,
you'd need to change this, probably borrowing the I_SPECIAL bit to
denote single-use. But this seems an unlikely thing to be doing.)

